<title>USA: Stryker damage award upheld.</title>
<headline>Stryker damage award upheld.</headline>
<dateline>KALAMAZOO, Mich. 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stryker Corp said the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit upheld a 1995 decision awarding Stryker $72.7 million in damages from Intermedics Orthopedics Inc.</p>
<p>Stryker alleged that Intermedics and its distributor infringed its U.S. patent on its OmniFlex Hip System.</p>
<p>Intermedics is a unit of Sulzer AG.</p>
